{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/325432-nwod-character-generator","id":325432,"title":"nWoD Character Generator ?!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-29T11:19:14-08:00","id":325432,"title":"nWoD Character Generator ?!?","content":"Ok so exalted has Anathema so i looked long and hard for a nWoD character Generator and I came across one that has not been updated in a long time. Vault of Darkness. So I tested it out and it looks good but needs some finishing touches added to it but the project has been stalled out... So that's why I am here. I am wondering if this a project that can picked up by someone else or is there something else free out there I have not found yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T04:14:38-08:00","id":326826,"title":"","content":"I found some files somewhere (I know that's not very helpful, sorry, got it from someone on the old White Wolf forums, might have been Mr. Gone) that added a large amount of the expanded nWoD line to Vault of Darkness, including Hunter and such. It seemed to work alright, but the printouts were kinda bland. However, Vault of Darkness is definitely not updated to The God Machine Chronicles, or for Blood &amp; Smoke/2e Vampire. At least as far as I am aware.<br /> <br /> Hero Lab was somewhat alright for nWoD, but the official development stalled on it for various reasons. With that said, there is a small community on the Lone Wolf Labs forums (the forums for the company that makes Hero Lab) that is making their own user-generated content for the nWoD data file. It would be easier if we had better access (such as template-access), but sadly we don't. A guy named RavenX has added a bunch of basic WoD content to it, and they've even added some GMC content, although it is not perfect. Still not bad though.<br /> <br /> You can find more info on it here: <a href=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=45487\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=45487</a><br /> <br /> And here: <a href=\"http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=49142\" target=\"_blank\">http://forums.wolflair.com/showthread.php?t=49142</a><br /> <br /> Hope that helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/819-vaneheart","name":"Vaneheart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar819_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-20T13:15:38-08:00","id":1556861,"title":"","content":"No really; any NWoD or CWoD NPC-generators or character-generators? I've got a few for V:tM and Dark Ages that I found, decades ago, but, I can't find any real ones now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-23T20:54:28-08:00","id":1556945,"title":"","content":"I think you can use AI for this nowadays. You just need to chose one and learn how to prompt it into doing what you want.<br /> <br /> ChatGPT, DeepSeek and Copilot are good choices for this task, albeit with distinct strengths. ChatGPT is practically ready-to-use for this, but will have lots of hiccups, so you should revise every output. DeepSeek is good with following complex structure, so you can make it work on your specifications quite well (I'll maybe devise a system for this on it later), but it's not the pinnacle of creativity and takes work. Copilot, if you have the Office 365 subscription, has the distinct advantage of being able to read your files without much of a hassle, so depending on your digital sources you can easily use non-public material, but then it's the paid option of the three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T13:34:41-07:00","id":1561736,"title":"","content":"I'm curious why someone reacted with nausea by me suggesting using AI <i><u>for a character generator</u></i>. That's... kind of an AI anyway.<br /> <br /> But I'll possibly be soon posting here some work I'm doing in this regard, only with free tier services. Starting with V5 because it's what I'm playing, but will adapt at least to CofD 2nd Ed and WoD20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T14:13:07-07:00","id":1561737,"title":"","content":"1) While it's not helpful, it is pretty obvious that a lot of people have strong negative feelings around the topic; esp. when it comes to creative spaces over technical ones.<br /> <br /> 2) Depending on the features someone wants out of a char-gen program, I don't really see the benefit of them to the task. 99% is something you can do with any spreadsheet program and some basic calculation knowledge: people want to enter their dots, Beats, and XP and make sure the math is right, then set derived stats (like Speed, WP, and Health in CofD 2e) auto-fill into appropriate fields. Maybe have some common dice-pools auto-fill as well. The biggest effort is if you're going to have the names of pre-existing things like Merits that you need to catalogue the names and point values of.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are programs that can do that work for you, but it's not difficult work, and the time spent babysitting so they don't mess things up is going to be fairly equal to the effort of doing the repetitive parts yourself (having done versions myself for CofD 1e).<br /> <br /> If people were looking for something more akin to a full NPC generator where concept and stats were something they wanted automated... I think that's more where the tools in question would actually have some value; even if like many people I don't value that application of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T21:25:20-07:00","id":1561754,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression it was exactly about a full NPC generator. And I value them as seed for imagination or a means to have stats without my perfectionism kicking in. My most recent character I didn't control it has already a more than 30 pages sheet and maybe 60+ of work.<br /> <br /> Haven't associated the word 'generator' with a sheet manager/automation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T02:32:49-07:00","id":1561758,"title":"","content":"While more speculation than I'd like, I think character-generator and sheet manager/automation largely stemmed from early applications to more meat-grinder oriented D&amp;D play where there was a greater assumption of using randomized char-gen and thus a desire for automating the process.<br /> <br /> Both Anathema (a fan project for Exalted) and Hero Labs (a for profit product) started as PC sheet managers with some automation. Hero Labs does a lot more these days, but adding features is how a program adds value, etc. etc. So that's certainly the focus at the start of the thread (I mean, it's a short thread that didn't seem to take off).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-13T20:32:43-07:00","id":1564035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/325432-nwod-character-generator?p=1561758#post1561758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While more speculation than I'd like, I think character-generator and sheet manager/automation largely stemmed from early applications to more meat-grinder oriented D&amp;D play where there was a greater assumption of using randomized char-gen and thus a desire for automating the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not looking for WoD meat-grinder, just a program that assigns random-dots. I'm detailed-oriented, but not THAT, detailed in which I have to outline every NPC; but, I do love creating Mortals for Masquerade to interact with the vampires; after all, that's what the game's about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-11-02T12:27:26-08:00","id":1565083,"title":"","content":"the only things I found AI are really good for in character creation are for soundboarding when you don't have anyone currently available to talk to, and to get randomized feedback with the right prompts, and image and sound generation. <br /> Can't afford to have every run-of-the-mill npc comissioned, that's a privilige you keep for important things. Still, I find giving a face to a minor character (or mangy, pestilence-stricken werewolf) can help quite a bit (both the players, and me when I ST, actually), and I have used e.g. ChatGPT for somewhat prettier DnD maps etc than I usually used (like, literally upload my paint-made map, tell it what style it should be in, good enough to go). It mostly supports a little what was already done, rather than truly add anything. And I think that's good enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}